{"type":"Feature","properties":{"id":"cp-benicia-waterfront","system":"central-pacific","name":"Benicia, the ferry slip to the line near Army Point","opened":"1879-12-28","closed":null,"structure":"surface","sources":[{"source":"ca-brc-report-10","supports":["opened"],"pages":"10","note":"\"to Suisun, December 28, 1879\"."},{"source":"usgs-benicia-1952","supports":["route"],"note":"Labelled Southern Pacific, along Benicia's waterfront."},{"source":"usgs-karquines-1898","supports":["geometry"]},{"source":"ohm-2026-10-15","supports":["geometry"],"note":"Ways 200464960"}],"flags":["closed_unsourced"],"notes":"From the slip along Benicia's waterfront to the main line, which today's track joins near Army Point. Trains to Sacramento left it for the bridge in 1930; when it last carried passengers isn't sourced.","geometry_confidence":"surveyed","geometry_method":"OpenHistoricalMap way 200464960 (CC0, as of 2026-10-15), which OHM's mappers drew from USGS Napa CA 1902 topographic map, cut to -122.12801,38.04760; checked on USGS Karquines 1:62,500 (1898) and USGS Benicia 1:24,000 (1952). Cut where it meets today's track near Army Point. OpenHistoricalMap's way was traced from the 1902 Napa sheet (1:125,000); on the 1952 sheet it lies along the waterfront track."},"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-122.164852,38.044654],[-122.164404,38.044511],[-122.157918,38.044252],[-122.147442,38.043829],[-122.139812,38.043558],[-122.137654,38.043759],[-122.132687,38.044275],[-122.131688,38.04446],[-122.130966,38.044673],[-122.130197,38.045056],[-122.12939,38.045595],[-122.128772,38.046184],[-122.128335,38.046877],[-122.128005,38.047605]]}},
